# Code Quality Standards

## Comments
- Add concise, meaningful comments for all methods and functions
- Comments should explain **why**, not **what** (code should be self-explanatory)
- Keep comments short and to the point
- Update comments when code changes

## Documentation
- Refrain from using emoji in documentation
- Put individual services into their own .md file linked from the README.md

## Best Practices
- Always follow framework-specific best practices
- Write DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) code
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Implement proper error handling and validation
- Follow SOLID principles where applicable
- Write testable code
